{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result so far is config_016 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + concat, singleprofile) at 0.535 acc / 0.519 F1, with config_008 (same but resnet50) at 0.527. RNA alone (pca_n2000) achieves 0.485, showing RNA is the dominant modality. However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA n2000, a linear method) and one image encoder pair. The most critical untested design axis is the RNA representation: does a learned deep encoder (scgpt) outperform linear PCA? Uncertainty: It is unclear whether the RNA bottleneck is in the encoding method or elsewhere. Question tested: config_031 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + concat, singleprofile) is a clean single-variable swap from config_016, isolating the effect of RNA encoder (pca_n2000 → scgpt) while holding image encoder, fusion, and profile setting constant. Why this is the best next experiment: Under limited budget, resolving whether a learned generative RNA encoder meaningfully improves over PCA is the highest-information single experiment. If scgpt substantially outperforms PCA, it redirects the search toward learned encoders and multiprofile transformer aggregation. If it does not, PCA is near-optimal and we can confidently invest remaining budget in fusion strategy, multiprofile aggregation, or image encoder choices. This avoids confounding multiple variables and directly extends our strongest evidence."
}

